    "content": "Tax Day 2026 is Wednesday, April 15, 2026. Individuals must file their 2025 federal income tax returns and pay any taxes owed by this date to avoid penalties. The IRS began accepting electronic returns on January 26, 2026. Taxpayers needing extra time can request an extension until October 15, 2026, but taxes owed must still be paid by April 15, 2026.Key 2026 Tax InformationDeadline: Tax returns for individuals are due April 15, 2026.Extension: File Form 4868 to get an extension until October 15, 2026.Where to File: Use IRS Free File or electronic filing for faster processing.Refunds: Many taxpayers are anticipated to receive larger refunds this year due to tax changes.Tax Day Deals and Freebies (April 15, 2026)Several companies are offering special deals on April 15:Krispy Kreme: Buy a dozen doughnuts and get an Original Glazed dozen free with code TAXBREAK.Wendy's: Free 6-piece nuggets with a $5 purchase via their app.QDOBA: Rewards members can get a $5 reward towards an entrée.7-Eleven: $10.40 off delivery orders of $25 or more with code WRITEOFF.Subway: Deals on sandwiches are available to reward members.For personalized tax advice, it is best to check the IRS website or consult a tax professional.",
